WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
Home service businesses are one of the

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.480
best ways that you can build real

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.120
wealth, but not all of them are created

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.080
equal. Some of these businesses look

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.160
great on the surface, but most people

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.720
who start them don't make it past year

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.920
two. So, today I'm going to be breaking

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.480
down the five worst home service

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:19.760
businesses to start from scratch in 2026

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.040
and exactly why they're so difficult to

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.520
get off the ground. And my name is

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.680
Austin Zeeback and I've been building

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.160
businesses for over a decade across real

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.800
estate, pest control, and a couple of

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.240
others. And if you get any value from

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.920
the video today at all, do me a huge

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.759
favor and just smash that like button.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.200
It really does help me out a ton and

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.640
it'll get this video in front of more

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.840
people who need to see it. So, getting

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:39.400
into it, the first business is roofing

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.480
and it's one of the most attractive

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:43.840
industries on paper. Storm damage

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.960
creates instant demand, ticket sizes are

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.520
really high, and homeowners aren't ever

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.560
doing the work themselves. And I

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.880
personally know roofing operators doing

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:54.000
seven and eight figures, so the money is

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:56.280
100% there. But, let's just look at the

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.480
market a little bit. So, as of 2026,

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.760
there are roughly 108,000

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.560
roofing contractor businesses operating

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:06.000
in the US. And that number has been

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.680
growing at 3.4% per year for the last 5

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.920
years. So, you are entering an

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:12.400
incredibly saturated market as a brand

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.880
new company with zero reputation and

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.840
zero reviews against operators who have

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.600
been around for years. And before you

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.440
can even compete, you need a state's

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.960
contractor's license, liability

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:25.160
insurance, a surety bond, and business

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.120
registration. And the licensing alone

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:28.840
takes a lot of time and a lot of money

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.560
before you even get started. Then

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.720
there's the business model question. And

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.160
this is something that most people

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.800
really never think about before they

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.720
actually start. There are essentially

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.480
two different ways to operate a roofing

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.760
company. You either work primarily off

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.800
of insurance claims or you go directly

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:44.840
to homeowners. And both come with their

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.360
own complications. The insurance route

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:48.240
can be a grind because insurance

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:49.400
companies don't want to pay right away

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.480
and they really don't want to pay at

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.680
all. They delay, they dispute, and they

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.520
drag out the entire process. And I

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.920
personally know operators who have had

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.760
claims held up for an entire year. And

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.840
that is a cash flow nightmare when

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.680
you've got and you have a bunch of

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.200
overhead that you have to cover. So, say

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.120
a homeowner wants to sell their house,

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.119
but the roof is old and they don't have

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.800
the $15,000 just sitting in their

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:12.720
checking account. He'll go ahead and

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.160
he'll actually front the cost to replace

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.720
the roof and he will get paid out of the

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:20.040
proceeds of the sale when the deal

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:21.640
closes by the escrow company. And it's a

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.240
smart model, but it requires you to

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.920
understand a completely different

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.720
payment process and you have to build

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.200
relationships with title companies and

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.440
real estate agents to make it work. And

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:33.040
not to mention, you have to have enough

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.440
cash to be able to front the cost of the

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.520
actual roof itself and potentially not

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:39.080
get paid for up to 30 days. According to

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.920
the Small Business Administration,

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:44.040
approximately 80% of roofing contractors

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:47.280
fail within the first 2 years. And

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:48.960
within 5 years, 96% are completely out

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.640
of the game. And the number one driver

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:54.120
is cash flow mismanagement. The pattern

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.440
is almost always the exact same. Someone

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.680
who is great at roofing decides to start

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.640
a roofing company. They're a craftsman,

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:02.320
but they're not a businessman. They

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.960
overspend on things like trucks and

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.920
equipment early on. They don't track

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.680
their numbers, they mismanage their cash

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.120
flow, and by the time they realize it,

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.400
their balance sheet is already in the

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.120
red and their P&L is just effed. And

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:15.440
things like bad customer service and

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.280
poor quality work accelerate that fall.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.680
Roofing can make you very wealthy, but

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.160
the failure rate should tell you

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:22.360
everything that you need to know about

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:24.560
how hard it is to build the business

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:26.720
from scratch. Okay, the second business

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.480
is hardscape. Now, hardscaping is a

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.480
premium service. You're talking about

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.320
patios, retaining walls, outdoor

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.440
kitchens, pergolas. These are

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:36.160
high-ticket projects with really strong

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.240
margins. And I actually got a quote on

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.400
my own backyard from a hardscape company

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:41.400
and I'll show you what that looks like

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:44.200
right here. The quote was over 100

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.520
grand, not including my pool. Homeowners

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.160
are willing to make that kind of

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.760
investment because they see it as

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.840
building equity in their home a lot of

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.840
times. And the margins in this industry

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:54.760
are kind of shocking. But, the scope of

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:56.760
these projects is also extremely

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:58.680
detailed and this isn't a service where

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.480
you can just figure it out as you go.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:02.760
The skill and the knowledge required to

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.440
execute at that level is significant and

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.440
customers spending that kind of money

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.680
expect that level of service. Then

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:09.760
there's the equipment side of things.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.360
So, to run a hardscape operation, you

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.920
probably are going to need some heavy

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.080
equipment. You're going to need tractors

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:17.440
and trailers and all kinds of stuff.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:19.799
We're talking 50 to 100 grand or even

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.600
more just to have the capability to take

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:23.120
on some of these bigger jobs. And that's

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:25.280
before you paid for insurance,

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:27.120
licensing, or a single employee. And

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.920
unlike pest control or lawn care where

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.680
you can build recurring revenue,

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:32.960
hardscape is almost entirely

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.680
project-based and all one-time revenue.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:36.120
You finish a job and you move on. You

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:38.200
never talk to them again, probably.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.040
There is no automatic next customer

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:41.760
waiting for you, so you're constantly

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:44.000
out there having to sell yourself on

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:46.600
every potential job site. Then you layer

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.280
on seasonality. Spring, summer, and fall

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.840
are typically your window of opportunity

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.720
depending on where you live. Winter

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:53.720
shuts a lot of the work down. So, when

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:55.760
you add it all up, high capital just to

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:57.880
get in the door, no recurring revenue to

00:04:55.760 --> 00:05:00.480
fall back on, and the reality of running

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:02.520
a seasonal business in most markets, I'd

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.280
say really difficult company to get off

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.800
the ground from scratch. And compared to

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:07.120
the majority of other home service

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:09.280
companies that you could start, you're

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:11.480
facing a much steeper uphill battle from

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.360
day one. And that is why this business

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:15.920
made the list for me. Okay, the third

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:17.640
business is garage improvement and this

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.360
is a legitimate and growing market.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:21.400
Homeowners are spending a ton of money

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:23.320
turning their garages into functional,

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.120
good-looking spaces. But, this isn't a

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:27.240
business that you can just jump into

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:29.200
cold. Unlike pressure washing or junk

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:31.360
removal where the barrier to get started

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:33.320
is pretty low, garage improvement

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.040
requires real level of skill and

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:37.200
knowledge before you can actually call

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.120
yourself a trusted service provider.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.360
Epoxy floor coatings, cabinet

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.680
installations, overhead storage systems,

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.080
garage door install and repair. These

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:46.920
aren't things that you kind of figure

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:48.520
out by just watching a YouTube video.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.160
Then there's all the licensing. So,

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:52.120
depending on your state where you live

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.120
and what services you offer, you may

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:56.040
need a contractor's license before you

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:58.320
can even legally operate. Garage door

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:00.520
installation, structural modifications,

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.320
and certain flooring applications can

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.080
carry their own requirements. And that

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:05.440
is a lot of friction before you've ever

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:07.400
even made a dollar. The things that

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.880
you're installing vary dramatically in

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.600
quality depending on where you're

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.280
actually sourcing them from. And if you

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:14.280
add in all the service vehicles, the

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:15.920
tools, and the product inventory before

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:18.000
you've even landed your first customer,

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:19.760
you're spending a lot of money without

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.400
making pretty much any money at the

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:22.960
beginning. Would I start a garage

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.480
improvement company from scratch if I

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.880
was getting into home services for the

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:29.320
first time? Probably not. It definitely

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.080
would not be my first choice. But, if

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:33.200
you spent time in the industry and you

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:35.200
know the work, starting a solo operation

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.080
can make sense. You don't need to go out

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.440
and buy brand new equipment and a shiny

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.200
wrapped truck on day one. You can start

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.960
lean with a used vehicle, used

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.640
equipment, and keep your overhead really

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.040
low until you scale and then you

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:48.080
eventually have more capital to work

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:50.480
with. The next business is considered

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:52.320
one of the core big four skilled trades

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:54.480
in construction. And there's a narrative

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.160
out there that plumbing is a dying trade

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.800
because of fewer young people entering

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.800
the field. And then you have the aging

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:01.280
workforce and the industry overall is

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:03.480
just shrinking. But, that is not what

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:06.000
the data says at all. The dying trade

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:08.400
narrative is not accurate. The demand is

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.920
very much alive. The reality is fewer

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.880
young people have entered the trade over

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:14.240
the past two decades, which has actually

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.920
created more opportunity, not less. And

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:18.240
the demand is not going anywhere.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:20.160
Building codes require licensed plumbers

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.800
for most of the installation and repair

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.840
work. And homeowners can swap out a

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:25.760
faucet, but anything involving supply

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:28.000
lines, drainage modifications, or

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:29.680
structural changes requires permanent

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.840
work completely by a licensed

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:34.440
professional. That regulatory protection

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:36.520
means you can't be displaced by DIY or

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:38.760
unlicensed competition and your work

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:40.520
will always exist. So, why did this make

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:44.040
my list? Well, there are roughly about

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:45.840
480,000 licensed plumbers in the US. And

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:47.600
that industry cannot keep up with

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:49.800
demand. And that sounds like a huge

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:51.600
opportunity on paper and it is if you're

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:53.320
already a licensed plumber. But, if

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:54.840
you're not, the path to owning a

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:56.680
plumbing company is much more

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:58.680
complicated than you might realize. You

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:00.920
generally don't need a personal master

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:03.520
plumber license to own the business, but

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:05.600
you do need to employ a licensed master

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:07.720
plumber to oversee all the technical

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.480
work within your business and to pull

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:11.280
permits and keep you compliant with

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:13.720
state law. That means that your entire

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:16.160
operation depends on finding and keeping

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:18.600
the right person before you can reliably

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:20.200
take on work. And finding that person is

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.720
your first real problem. You're

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:24.080
competing with every other plumbing

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:25.960
company to hire from a very small pool

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:27.320
of licensed talent. And that same

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:29.320
shortage that makes the industry

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.680
attractive makes staffing it one of the

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.560
hardest challenges that you're going to

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:34.560
face early on. Then there's the failure

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:37.599
rate. Estimates suggest contractor

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:39.680
failure rates as high as 70 to 95%

00:08:37.599 --> 00:08:41.680
driven by the same issues that kill most

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:43.800
trades in business, which is poor

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:45.640
management, cash flow problems, and

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:47.320
taking on the wrong customers. The

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:49.120
demand is real. The regulatory

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.640
protection is real. But, getting the

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:52.560
right people in the right place,

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:55.040
managing your cash flow, and building an

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:57.160
operation that can actually scale is

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.040
where most people come up short and that

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:01.200
is exactly why it made my list. The

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.640
final business on my list is HVAC and

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.560
it's probably the most attractive one on

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.560
the list. It is essential, it is

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:09.240
year-round, the tickets are high, and

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:11.040
there will never be a shortage of

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:13.120
demand. Now, I'm not here to tell you

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:14.920
HVAC is a bad business. It's actually

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:16.960
one of the best ones that you can own.

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:18.800
But, starting one from scratch is one of

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.880
the hardest things that you can do in

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:22.640
the home service space. Before you spend

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:24.440
a single dollar, you need to build out

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:27.000
what your company looks like on paper.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:28.760
Vans, tools, salaries, benefits,

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:31.000
staffing. You'll need to get really

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:32.720
clear on your cost per hour to run a

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.360
technician in the field because that

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:35.920
number will drive everything. And when

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:38.480
you start running these numbers, the

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:40.720
startup cost gets very real very fast. A

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:43.200
lean solo operation can get started

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:44.920
anywhere from probably 10 to 50 grand,

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:46.560
but if you want to build a real company

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:48.960
with multiple technicians, you're

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:50.640
looking at well over 100 grand. And then

